{"term":"transplant","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:440f41954207030393","definition":"To uproot (a growing plant), and plant it in another place.","example":"Vanilla itself was transplanted from Madagascar, the main source of the spice, to Polynesia a century ago.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["isotransplanted","nontransplanted","retransplant","transplantability","transplantable","untransplanted","xenotransplanted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transplant#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eb69679cb13c61a7b0","definition":"To remove (something) and establish its residence in another place; to resettle or relocate.","example":"But after half a year the Russian Government prohibited its circulation, and as a consequence the paper ceased to appear. He then went to Tschernowitz and started a Folksblatt. Upon the advice of a friend he transplanted his paper to Jassy, Roumania.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["isotransplanted","nontransplanted","retransplant","transplantability","transplantable","untransplanted","xenotransplanted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transplant#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:99eb4571441e200900","definition":"To transfer (tissue or an organ) from one body to another, or from one part of a body to another.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["isotransplanted","nontransplanted","retransplant","transplantability","transplantable","untransplanted","xenotransplanted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https